1
00:00:05,060 --> 00:00:09,060
The Hamon has almost
reached my head and brain!

2
00:00:09,420 --> 00:00:11,037
We must do something!

3
00:00:11,120 --> 00:00:12,880
Move our move!

4
00:00:32,320 --> 00:00:35,080
Lordeo, we'll get a new body for you.

5
00:00:42,720 --> 00:00:47,060
Excerpt from the December 4th,
1888 edition of the London Press.

6
00:00:47,720 --> 00:00:52,297
It has been reported that 73
of the 452 residents in the

7
00:00:52,380 --> 00:00:55,556
town of Wind Knight's lot
have gone missing overnight.

8
00:00:56,380 --> 00:01:01,240
The police have been pursuing lines of
inquiry based on certain witness accounts.

9
00:01:02,480 --> 00:01:05,437
These accounts state that
four outsiders were seen

10
00:01:05,520 --> 00:01:08,755
burning a man's clothing at
the base of a nearby cliff.

11
00:01:09,020 --> 00:01:11,437
One of the four was
reportedly wielding a large

12
00:01:11,520 --> 00:01:14,860
hammer and using it to
smash a curious stone mask.

13
00:01:16,520 --> 00:01:18,380
Our work here is done.

14
00:01:34,320 --> 00:01:35,897
Thank you

15
00:01:35,980 --> 00:01:42,980
so

16
00:01:53,080 --> 00:01:55,400
much for watching.

17
00:02:29,840 --> 00:02:33,180
in the future...

18
00:02:34,740 --> 00:02:36,820
I'll die! I'll go!

19
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:56,000
Heir to the Joestar fortune,
Jonathan Joestar weds Arena.

20
00:02:56,560 --> 00:02:58,442
Only daughter of the Pendletons.

21
00:02:59,240 --> 00:03:02,400
A couple will travel to the Americas.

22
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:03,830
Nice.

23
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:05,830
Blazes!

24
00:03:06,240 --> 00:03:08,000
Look what time it is!

25
00:03:08,780 --> 00:03:10,660
Their ship's about to leave!

26
00:03:15,460 --> 00:03:16,290
Oi!

27
00:03:17,180 --> 00:03:18,740
Mr. Speedwagon!

28
00:03:18,980 --> 00:03:21,580
You almost missed being
able to say goodbye.

29
00:03:21,980 --> 00:03:23,480
Sorry I'm so late.

30
00:03:23,680 --> 00:03:25,037
So then, where are they?

31
00:03:25,120 --> 00:03:26,944
They're both on board the ship.

32
00:03:27,820 --> 00:03:29,291
It's about ready to sail.

33
00:03:30,080 --> 00:03:31,160
What? It is?

34
00:03:31,300 --> 00:03:32,200
Where are they?

35
00:03:32,320 --> 00:03:33,555
I've got to see them!

36
00:03:34,220 --> 00:03:39,360
Now then, Father Sticks, we expect to hear
great things from your mission to Mexico.

37
00:03:40,700 --> 00:03:42,406
I'll certainly do what I can.

38
00:03:44,560 --> 00:03:45,600
Jonathan Joestar!

39
00:03:45,740 --> 00:03:46,900
Where are you?

40
00:03:47,120 --> 00:03:48,537
Watch where you're going!

41
00:03:48,620 --> 00:03:51,385
What makes this thing so
blasted heavy, anyway?

42
00:03:51,760 --> 00:03:52,677
How should I know?

43
00:03:52,760 --> 00:03:56,642
We've been hired by that Asian
bloke, so we move it where he says.

44
00:04:02,620 --> 00:04:05,000
Boy, did you boys hear that?

45
00:04:05,180 --> 00:04:07,360
Quit flapping your blasted cake hole.

46
00:04:07,660 --> 00:04:08,500
Now move it.

47
00:04:08,620 --> 00:04:10,914
We don't get paid till this job's done.

48
00:04:13,860 --> 00:04:14,690
Ow!

49
00:04:14,800 --> 00:04:17,580
Ruddy hooligans! Mr. Speedwagon? Hmm?

50
00:04:17,840 --> 00:04:20,260
Look, they're up there. Hello?

51
00:04:21,960 --> 00:04:22,790
Jonathan!

52
00:04:25,220 --> 00:04:26,800
What a beautiful sight.

53
00:04:27,340 --> 00:04:29,760
I wish you a long, love-filled life.

54
00:04:30,440 --> 00:04:32,220
I'll always be here for you.

55
00:04:32,660 --> 00:04:34,520
If you ever need me, just call.

56
00:04:34,820 --> 00:04:35,760
I'll be there.

57
00:04:37,100 --> 00:04:40,041
Though, at the moment, I'd
just be in the way, eh?

58
00:04:48,980 --> 00:04:49,940
Bon voyage!

59
00:04:51,200 --> 00:04:53,320
Have a wonderful trip!

60
00:05:23,080 --> 00:05:25,000
Poor little bird all alone.

61
00:05:25,340 --> 00:05:26,740
Did you lose your flop?

62
00:05:35,000 --> 00:05:35,830
Iran.

63
00:05:36,820 --> 00:05:38,114
Something wrong, love?

64
00:05:42,440 --> 00:05:44,322
Dear, what are you crying about?

65
00:05:44,740 --> 00:05:47,152
These tears that I'm crying are from joy.

66
00:05:47,480 --> 00:05:49,320
Joy that I am here with you.

67
00:05:51,660 --> 00:05:54,740
Even as a boy, you strove
to be a true gentleman,

68
00:05:55,140 --> 00:05:58,740
a champion of others, no matter
the consequence to yourself.

69
00:05:59,100 --> 00:06:04,400
And now that proud and noble
Jonathan Joestar is here in my arms.

70
00:06:04,640 --> 00:06:05,900
And I have you.

71
00:06:06,400 --> 00:06:11,680
When my heart was frozen in despair, you
warmed me and brought me back to life.

72
00:06:12,920 --> 00:06:16,660
I am fortunate to have saved
a world that has you in it.

73
00:06:17,160 --> 00:06:20,240
I only wish Father could have known you.

74
00:06:22,540 --> 00:06:23,440
Iran, come.

75
00:06:23,780 --> 00:06:25,720
Supper's waiting. Jonathan!

76
00:06:28,420 --> 00:06:32,538
Um, I wanted to tell you to be careful
so you wouldn't bash your head.

77
00:06:38,720 --> 00:06:41,880
I wish that today would last forever.

78
00:06:47,920 --> 00:06:48,750
Damn!

79
00:06:48,920 --> 00:06:50,317
It fell into the engine room.

80
00:06:50,400 --> 00:06:53,000
That's a filthy place to go after it.

81
00:06:54,180 --> 00:06:57,820
I could just sell it, but
it brings in the shackles.

82
00:06:59,580 --> 00:07:00,720
Dear Lord.

83
00:07:01,340 --> 00:07:04,440
You surely do seem to enjoy picking on me.

84
00:07:12,400 --> 00:07:13,580
Oh, no.

85
00:07:13,860 --> 00:07:16,580
I haven't the experience
drinking Amanda's.

86
00:07:16,700 --> 00:07:17,760
Just a bit.

87
00:07:18,220 --> 00:07:19,897
Barely enough to get the taste.

88
00:07:19,980 --> 00:07:21,960
It really isn't strong at all.

89
00:07:22,300 --> 00:07:23,720
I think it's good.

90
00:07:25,940 --> 00:07:26,770
Here.

91
00:07:39,240 --> 00:07:41,240
No, it can't be!

92
00:07:50,100 --> 00:07:50,930
Jonathan?

93
00:07:52,200 --> 00:07:53,030
Impossible!

94
00:07:53,220 --> 00:07:54,660
There is no way!

95
00:07:55,440 --> 00:07:56,270
He's here!

96
00:07:56,380 --> 00:07:57,280
Dio's alive!

97
00:08:00,340 --> 00:08:01,320
Arena, go!

98
00:08:01,520 --> 00:08:02,873
Back to our cabin, now!

99
00:08:03,120 --> 00:08:05,120
And don't forget to lock the door!

100
00:08:14,700 --> 00:08:15,530
Hmph.

101
00:08:16,520 --> 00:08:17,350
Eh?

102
00:08:17,433 --> 00:08:18,900
Well, that's rather strange.

103
00:08:19,220 --> 00:08:20,580
The lock's undone.

104
00:08:21,400 --> 00:08:22,694
Queer bit of business.

105
00:08:23,020 --> 00:08:26,480
I can see a metal catch
glinting on the inside there.

106
00:08:26,740 --> 00:08:27,837
But that...

107
00:08:27,920 --> 00:08:28,897
would mean...

108
00:08:28,980 --> 00:08:31,451
That this trunk is locked from the inside!

109
00:08:37,800 --> 00:08:38,760
Halt!

110
00:08:39,520 --> 00:08:41,220
You can't escape!

111
00:08:42,800 --> 00:08:46,100
Where is my body?

112
00:08:47,060 --> 00:08:47,890
Dish!

113
00:08:48,580 --> 00:08:50,820
Jonathan is so upset.

114
00:08:51,120 --> 00:08:52,360
Something is wrong.

115
00:08:56,700 --> 00:09:00,900
Jojo, do you see the condition
in which I find myself?

116
00:09:01,460 --> 00:09:02,760
Your work.

117
00:09:03,400 --> 00:09:06,480
There is a reason I display
myself to you like this.

118
00:09:06,960 --> 00:09:10,700
Why would I show my weakness
to my deadliest foe?

119
00:09:11,420 --> 00:09:16,697
Because though I once despised you,
now I have only the greatest respect.

120
00:09:16,780 --> 00:09:20,780
For your spirit, your valor
in battle, your power.

121
00:09:21,180 --> 00:09:22,360
I see it now.

122
00:09:23,360 --> 00:09:27,160
How incredible you are, Tio. Jojo.

123
00:09:27,980 --> 00:09:28,810
No.

124
00:09:28,893 --> 00:09:32,760
If not for you, I would never have
obtained the power of the Stone Mask.

125
00:09:34,840 --> 00:09:38,520
However, your damnable meddling
cost me world domination.

126
00:09:39,040 --> 00:09:43,140
If there really is a god, one who
plucks the strings of our fate,

127
00:09:43,400 --> 00:09:47,260
I am certain that our fates were
bound together for a reason.

128
00:09:49,740 --> 00:09:54,097
Our two existences were only
ever intended to be but one.

129
00:09:54,180 --> 00:09:58,880
And so I will take the body of
the only man on earth I respect.

130
00:09:59,200 --> 00:10:01,520
Then I will live in eternal glory.

131
00:10:01,760 --> 00:10:05,100
For that is the destiny
which is waiting for me.

132
00:10:05,400 --> 00:10:06,694
There will be no pain.

133
00:10:06,940 --> 00:10:09,600
That is the final gift I bequeath to you.

134
00:10:10,760 --> 00:10:13,320
No, no, those eyes, I can't.

135
00:10:13,600 --> 00:10:16,640
Live on as my body, Jojo.

136
00:10:19,040 --> 00:10:20,100
Jonathan, what?

137
00:10:21,640 --> 00:10:22,470
Freedom!

138
00:10:46,100 --> 00:10:47,460
No! Jonathan!

139
00:10:51,880 --> 00:10:54,397
Oh, a pity you wouldn't hear me?

140
00:10:54,480 --> 00:10:57,297
If only you had remained
still as I told you!

141
00:10:57,380 --> 00:11:00,439
Your death, in fact, would
have been quite painless.

142
00:11:01,540 --> 00:11:04,077
Torn from your little
fairy tale into hell!

143
00:11:04,160 --> 00:11:06,937
Thrust into a reality
you didn't know existed.

144
00:11:07,020 --> 00:11:08,920
What will you do now?

145
00:11:10,000 --> 00:11:12,420
Did Jojo never tell you of me?

146
00:11:12,740 --> 00:11:18,080
The evil that dwells there in the darkness
I may not look like much right now,

147
00:11:18,420 --> 00:11:20,220
but surely you remember me.

148
00:11:21,000 --> 00:11:22,300
Iran Pendleton.

149
00:11:22,740 --> 00:11:27,560
Wait, it's Iran Joestar
now, isn't it? Dio!

150
00:11:31,240 --> 00:11:33,560
The ship's full of bonkers!

151
00:11:56,620 --> 00:12:00,580
As you ordered, Lord, I drained
the life of only one passenger.

152
00:12:00,880 --> 00:12:04,520
And now most of the ship has
joined our little family.

153
00:12:06,900 --> 00:12:09,740
And now we will proceed to America.

154
00:12:10,060 --> 00:12:11,780
Isn't that right, Lord Dio?

155
00:12:12,000 --> 00:12:13,117
I can't speak.

156
00:12:13,200 --> 00:12:16,160
I can't even take a breath.

157
00:12:16,460 --> 00:12:18,400
I have to move.

158
00:12:19,900 --> 00:12:20,730
Lorena.

159
00:12:20,813 --> 00:12:21,643
Lorena!

160
00:12:23,020 --> 00:12:25,320
I have to save.

161
00:12:30,000 --> 00:12:31,600
Can't gather.

162
00:12:32,120 --> 00:12:32,950
Hormone.

163
00:12:34,000 --> 00:12:36,540
Well, how the mighty have fallen.

164
00:12:36,960 --> 00:12:40,737
This sniveling whelp can't
even draw a proper breath now.

165
00:12:40,820 --> 00:12:44,260
Now, he'll be causing no more
mischief with his Hormone.

166
00:12:44,780 --> 00:12:47,700
This is what he gets for
crossing you, Lord Dio.

167
00:12:48,060 --> 00:12:49,860
Now we are going to play.

168
00:12:50,240 --> 00:12:53,160
Or maybe I'll just sit quietly and watch

169
00:12:53,880 --> 00:12:56,500
while he suffocates slowly, ha ha ha.

170
00:12:56,980 --> 00:12:58,220
Silence, Wang Chen.

171
00:12:58,660 --> 00:13:01,080
There shall be no insult to Jojo.

172
00:13:01,780 --> 00:13:05,960
He is the one man capable of
bringing me to the apex of my fate.

173
00:13:06,340 --> 00:13:08,697
You will show him all
the respect which is due

174
00:13:08,780 --> 00:13:11,940
to him by severing his
head in a painless manner.

175
00:13:12,300 --> 00:13:14,000
Of course, Lord Dio.

176
00:13:14,800 --> 00:13:20,120
The body of my dearest foe has
become my future! Jonathan!

177
00:13:25,440 --> 00:13:27,900
He's up to something. Be careful!

178
00:13:28,260 --> 00:13:31,580
He might have one last trick
up his muscle-bound sleeve.

179
00:13:32,360 --> 00:13:33,820
Bah, he's done for.

180
00:13:34,120 --> 00:13:37,080
Lord Dio overestimates his mighty power.

181
00:13:37,860 --> 00:13:39,680
Well, Jonathan Joestar,

182
00:13:40,000 --> 00:13:43,765
I'll scoop out what little brains
you have with my bare fingers.

183
00:13:45,440 --> 00:13:47,160
Must save Arena.

184
00:13:47,480 --> 00:13:52,540
I have to use the last bit of
hormone left in me all at once.

185
00:13:53,080 --> 00:13:54,360
Please work.

186
00:13:55,180 --> 00:13:56,010
Careful.

187
00:13:56,260 --> 00:13:57,460
Wang Chen, look out!

188
00:14:05,380 --> 00:14:08,637
something broke inside my body

189
00:14:08,720 --> 00:14:14,000
something important what have you done

190
00:14:19,500 --> 00:14:25,400
This is the end, the last Harmon I have.

191
00:14:25,800 --> 00:14:32,540
Too weak to destroy that zombie
completely, but it was enough.

192
00:14:39,220 --> 00:14:40,100
What?

193
00:14:40,300 --> 00:14:42,297
What is he playing at?

194
00:14:42,380 --> 00:14:45,560
Jojo has interfered with Wang Chen's body,

195
00:14:45,860 --> 00:14:49,960
disrupting its functions without
bringing it to complete destruction.

196
00:14:50,440 --> 00:14:53,900
He's made it seize tightly
onto a piece of machinery.

197
00:14:54,360 --> 00:15:00,920
And the device it clings to so
immovably is the paddle's screw shaft.

198
00:15:01,740 --> 00:15:05,300
The strength of a zombie is
sufficient to arrest the paddle.

199
00:15:06,140 --> 00:15:11,317
If the shaft is stopped, steam pressure
in the piston will build up inexorably.

200
00:15:11,400 --> 00:15:14,520
Under such conditions,
there is but one end.

201
00:15:14,900 --> 00:15:16,640
The ship will explode!

202
00:15:17,640 --> 00:15:19,880
Jonathan, what's happening?

203
00:15:20,600 --> 00:15:23,440
Why is this happening to us?

204
00:15:23,680 --> 00:15:26,280
You must leave, Iran.

205
00:15:26,760 --> 00:15:29,580
Soon the ship will be destroyed.

206
00:15:34,720 --> 00:15:39,340
I don't know how the things that
are occurring today are possible.

207
00:15:40,240 --> 00:15:42,580
It's all too impossible to bear.

208
00:15:42,860 --> 00:15:45,448
I don't know whether I
should cry or scream.

209
00:15:45,700 --> 00:15:48,935
Perhaps I should just faint
dead away and block it out.

210
00:15:51,020 --> 00:15:53,500
But there is one thing I know.

211
00:15:55,220 --> 00:15:59,960
Iran Joestar will remain with her husband.

212
00:16:03,920 --> 00:16:09,937
In the warmth of these lips I
feel the cool ebbing of his life

213
00:16:10,020 --> 00:16:15,197
Jonathan Joe Star is dying But we

214
00:16:15,280 --> 00:16:18,400
are together I want to stay like this

215
00:16:19,820 --> 00:16:22,897
Until the ship explodes and everything

216
00:16:22,980 --> 00:16:27,020
burns to ash until everything is gone?

217
00:16:48,220 --> 00:16:50,737
It's alright if you cry,

218
00:16:50,820 --> 00:16:56,380
but you have to stay alive and go on.

219
00:16:57,160 --> 00:16:59,540
Just like in a storybook.

220
00:16:59,960 --> 00:17:04,195
You want me to come to the aid of a
helpless child and escape to safety?

221
00:17:05,880 --> 00:17:06,980
That's unfair!

222
00:17:07,480 --> 00:17:08,598
Just sheer cruelty!

223
00:17:09,100 --> 00:17:13,360
The only thing that I want is
to end my life here with you.

224
00:17:14,400 --> 00:17:20,140
That woman died trying to
save her child until the last.

225
00:17:20,560 --> 00:17:24,320
My own mother did the same thing for me.

226
00:17:24,820 --> 00:17:25,980
Save yourself.

227
00:17:26,340 --> 00:17:28,500
Take the baby. Hurry!

228
00:17:32,840 --> 00:17:37,537
So your plan is to destroy
this vessel is it Jojo?

229
00:17:37,620 --> 00:17:40,457
You never give up or give
in, no matter the odds!

230
00:17:40,540 --> 00:17:44,237
But know this, determination
is not just in you.

231
00:17:44,320 --> 00:17:45,557
I will live.

232
00:17:45,640 --> 00:17:47,917
There is no one who can defy me.

233
00:17:48,000 --> 00:17:50,777
I will take your body as my own.

234
00:17:50,860 --> 00:17:53,000
Zombies hither!

235
00:17:55,600 --> 00:17:59,560
Devour Wang Chen's body and
restart the piston. Once you have?

236
00:18:04,260 --> 00:18:06,640
The end has begun.

237
00:18:22,020 --> 00:18:25,480
It's already blown apart,
but there's still a way out.

238
00:18:25,700 --> 00:18:28,977
I was protecting myself from
the sun's rays well before this.

239
00:18:29,060 --> 00:18:30,440
Let it explode.

240
00:18:30,900 --> 00:18:33,488
I already have everything
I need to survive.

241
00:18:38,600 --> 00:18:40,540
Iran, take a good look.

242
00:18:40,960 --> 00:18:43,720
Since Jojo can no longer use his ham on,

243
00:18:43,920 --> 00:18:47,140
I'll remove his head and
take his body as my own.

244
00:18:47,440 --> 00:18:51,320
Then I shall walk over and
lie down in my velvet boudoir.

245
00:18:51,660 --> 00:18:54,557
That humble shelter is
marvelously constructed.

246
00:18:54,640 --> 00:18:57,237
It could withstand a ton of dynamite.

247
00:18:57,320 --> 00:18:59,240
Goodbye, Jojo.

248
00:18:59,700 --> 00:19:03,940
And welcome to you, my new eternal body!

249
00:19:08,760 --> 00:19:09,590
Jonathan!

250
00:19:17,220 --> 00:19:18,050
Dio.

251
00:19:18,880 --> 00:19:23,260
As you observed, it may be true
that our fate is to be together.

252
00:19:24,020 --> 00:19:26,360
I feel an odd warmth for you.

253
00:19:27,320 --> 00:19:33,920
For now, our lives are interwoven completely
and will end along with this ship.

254
00:19:37,840 --> 00:19:41,640
Farewell to you, my beloved.

255
00:19:47,200 --> 00:19:49,540
Jojo, let me go!

256
00:19:50,360 --> 00:19:51,260
Release me!

257
00:19:51,540 --> 00:19:53,277
Think of what we two can achieve!

258
00:19:53,360 --> 00:19:55,817
You'd like a taste of
eternity, would you not?

259
00:19:55,900 --> 00:19:57,560
I can heal your wounds.

260
00:19:57,840 --> 00:20:00,380
You and Iran can live together forever!

261
00:20:02,100 --> 00:20:03,020
Jojo!

262
00:20:06,740 --> 00:20:07,577
No.

263
00:20:07,660 --> 00:20:08,900
It's too late.

264
00:20:10,080 --> 00:20:11,260
He's dead.

265
00:20:37,500 --> 00:20:42,960
Jonathan Joestar passed away
into undeserved oblivion.

266
00:20:43,880 --> 00:20:49,940
His life was an important part of
history, but invisible to ordinary people.

267
00:20:52,020 --> 00:20:55,657
Most of humanity for whom he sacrificed

268
00:20:55,740 --> 00:20:58,737
will never know of his
noble accomplishments,

269
00:20:58,820 --> 00:21:02,380
but his descendants will.

270
00:21:09,260 --> 00:21:16,220
The life within me, newly created by Jonathan
and I, will certainly hear his story.

271
00:21:21,460 --> 00:21:25,800
Arena Joestar was soon rescued
afloat near the Canary Islands,

272
00:21:26,240 --> 00:21:30,840
and the Book of the Stone
Mask was closed for a time.

273
00:21:31,300 --> 00:21:37,280
But that was only the beginning
of a new, bizarre adventure.

274
00:22:08,060 --> 00:22:11,337
I'll be the roundabout.

275
00:22:11,420 --> 00:22:15,497
The words will make you out and out.

276
00:22:15,580 --> 00:22:19,420
I spend the day your way.

277
00:22:20,680 --> 00:22:25,280
Call it morning driving through
the sun and in and out the valley.

278
00:22:35,120 --> 00:22:38,357
The music dance and sing.

279
00:22:38,440 --> 00:22:42,537
They make the children really ring.

280
00:22:42,620 --> 00:22:46,780
I spend the day your way.

281
00:22:47,980 --> 00:22:50,717
Cold in morning driving through the sun.

282
00:22:50,800 --> 00:22:52,560
And in and out the valley.

283
00:22:54,480 --> 00:22:57,140
In and out around the lake.

284
00:22:58,240 --> 00:23:00,597
Mountains come out of the sky.

285
00:23:00,680 --> 00:23:02,280
And they'll stand there.

286
00:23:05,320 --> 00:23:07,537
One mile over we'll be there.

287
00:23:07,620 --> 00:23:08,980
And we'll see you.

288
00:23:12,260 --> 00:23:14,017
22 summers, we'll be there.

289
00:23:14,100 --> 00:23:15,512
We'll be there with you.

290
00:23:18,920 --> 00:23:21,077
24 and 5, but we'll see.

291
00:23:21,160 --> 00:23:23,900
I'll be there with you.

292
00:23:28,100 --> 00:23:30,657
It was in the fall of 1938.

293
00:23:30,740 --> 00:23:33,037
It's good to see you again, Speedbucket.

294
00:23:33,120 --> 00:23:34,497
You bastard, how could you have possibly?

295
00:23:34,580 --> 00:23:35,557
Have known where they were?

296
00:23:35,640 --> 00:23:36,470
Teach him a lesson.

297
00:23:36,553 --> 00:23:37,597
Joseph Joestar.

298
00:23:37,680 --> 00:23:39,520
My friends call me JoJo.
